{
  "statement": "As the SafetyAgent, I emphasize that safety is paramount in the autonomous driving system. SAF-01 ensures a multi-layer safety architecture critical for collision protection and risk mitigation. SAF-02 mandates prompt execution of Minimal Risk Maneuvers to protect passengers during failures. SAF-03 enforces continuous monitoring of ODD compliance for safe operation. SAF-04 and SAF-05 focus on minimizing jerk and adhering to curvature constraints to prevent accidents. SAF-06 ensures reliable handling of obstacles, while SAF-07 allows for relaxation of smoothness constraints in emergencies, prioritizing safety. This holistic approach ensures the system can effectively manage safety risks while operating efficiently.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {
      "ids": ["EFF-03", "SAF-02"],
      "type": "logical",
      "description": "The requirement for Minimal Risk Maneuvers to be executed within 5 seconds (SAF-02) may conflict with the need for performance efficiency during such maneuvers (EFF-03), potentially compromising safety."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["EFF-07", "SAF-04"],
      "type": "logical",
      "description": "Minimizing jerk during normal operation (SAF-04) may contradict the need to prioritize smoothness during emergency maneuvers (EFF-07), which could affect passenger safety."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["TRU-06", "SAF-03"],
      "type": "resource",
      "description": "The requirement for secure remote updates (TRU-06) may impact the latency required for continuous monitoring of ODD compliance (SAF-03), affecting the system's ability to respond to safety-critical situations."
    }
  ],
